# Cursor Rules for Android Game Hub Project

## Project Overview
This is an Android game hub built with Jetpack Compose. The project contains:
- MainActivity: Game selection menu
- PixelCollectorGame: A 2D pixel collection game
- Future games can be added as separate activities

## Code Style & Standards
- Use Kotlin for all Android code
- Follow Android development best practices
- Use Jetpack Compose for UI components
- Maintain clean architecture principles
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Add proper comments for complex logic

## Game Development Rules
- Each game should be a separate Activity
- Use data classes for game state management
- Implement proper collision detection
- Maintain 60 FPS for smooth gameplay
- Use immutable state patterns where possible
- Handle lifecycle events properly

## File Organization
- Keep game logic separate from UI components
- Use proper package structure (com.baraka.game)
- Place new games in the main package
- Update AndroidManifest.xml for new activities
- Update MainActivity game selection when adding games

## Performance Guidelines
- Minimize object creation in game loops
- Use efficient data structures for game entities
- Avoid unnecessary recompositions in Compose
- Handle memory management for game objects
- Use appropriate coroutine scopes

## Testing & Quality
- Write unit tests for game logic
- Test on different screen sizes
- Ensure proper error handling
- Validate user input and game state
- Test game performance on target devices

## Future Game Ideas
- Platformer games
- Puzzle games
- Arcade-style games
- Card games
- Physics-based games

## Dependencies
- Use latest stable versions of Compose
- Follow Material 3 design guidelines
- Implement proper navigation between games
- Use appropriate Android lifecycle components
